    "body": "## Summary\n- add an authenticated batch endpoint for saved-job state across one discovery page\n- resolve up to 50 job ids in a single repository query instead of N+1 per-card status requests\n- deduplicate requested ids before persistence lookup and return only the ids saved by the current user\n- keep the existing single-job status endpoint for backwards compatibility\n- cover batching/deduplication in unit tests and document the API contract\n\n## API\n`GET /saved-jobs/status?jobIds=1,2,3`\n\nResponse:\n```json\n{\"savedJobIds\":[1,3]}\n```\n\nValidation requires 1..50 positive ids.\n\n## Safety / privacy\n- endpoint remains authenticated and scoped to the current user's bookmarks\n- no job details, exact locations or other users' bookmark state are exposed\n- no schema change is required; the existing `(user_id, job_id)` bookmark indexes/constraints are reused\n\n## Validation\nCI should run Maven tests, frontend lint/build, Flyway/PostgreSQL smokes and existing runtime gates. Do not merge unless required checks are green.",
